<item>
            <title>[LU-20834] lustre-initialization: client node not provisioned, lustre modules not loaded (mount: No such device)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20834</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;lustre-initialization failed because the Lustre client modules were never loaded on one client node. The cluster did not come up, so no test ran.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Session: &lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/cbfbf6f0-38f7-4209-998f-1055132f792f&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/cbfbf6f0-38f7-4209-998f-1055132f792f&lt;/a&gt; (review-dne-zfs-part-1, RHEL 10.1, trevis-156vm133..140)&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Mount of the client trevis-156vm134:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;2026-09-25T18:12:47 trevis-156vm134: mount.lustre: mount 10.240.46.238@tcp:/lustre at /mnt/lustre failed: No such device
2026-09-25T18:12:47 trevis-156vm134: Are the lustre modules loaded?
2026-09-25T18:12:47 Exit code: 19
2026-09-25T18:13:55 Auster exited unexpectedly
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;dmesg on trevis-156vm134 has no Lustre or LNet message at all, so lustre.ko was never loaded. The node&apos;s journal shows the provisioning job failing after boot:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Sep 25 18:08:06 trevis-156vm134 CROND[973]: (root) CMDOUT ([2026-09-25T18:08:06+00:00] FATAL: NoMethodError: undefined method `logger&apos; for nil:NilClass)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;This looks like a test-node setup problem, not a code problem. The same class was seen before on review-dne-zfs-part-2 and review-dne-zfs-part-6 (RHEL 10.1) in August 2026.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
