                            <comment id="503019" author="JIRAUSER21604" created="Thu, 8 Oct 2026 01:45:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;This also hits a server node, not only a client. On review-dne-part-1 (el10.1) for &lt;a href=&quot;https://review.whamcloud.com/68416&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/68416&lt;/a&gt; patch set 21, the second MDS never loaded the Lustre modules, while the first MDS on the same build did:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/bc4e777a-2456-4088-bd5a-6fc7c2d84d4d&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/bc4e777a-2456-4088-bd5a-6fc7c2d84d4d&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;preformatted panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;preformattedContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;Start mds2: mount -t lustre_tgt -o localrecov  /dev/mapper/mds2_flakey /mnt/lustre-mds2
trevis-152vm279: mount.lustre_tgt: mount /dev/mapper/mds2_flakey at /mnt/lustre-mds2 failed: No such device
trevis-152vm279: Are the lustre modules loaded?
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;p&gt;trevis-152vm279 (mds2) booted &lt;tt&gt;6.12.0-124.56.1.el10_1_lustre&lt;/tt&gt;, but its dmesg has no &lt;tt&gt;Lustre: Build Version&lt;/tt&gt; line. trevis-152vm268 (mds1) has &lt;tt&gt;Lustre: Lustre: Build Version: 2.17.58_50_g34bea41&lt;/tt&gt; and mounted &lt;tt&gt;lustre-MDT0000&lt;/tt&gt; a few seconds earlier.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
